## 🎯 **Four-Layer Component Architecture**

### **Layer Structure**

1. **Service** (`component-name-service.ts`) - Business logic, state calculations
2. **Controller** (`component-name-controller.ts`) - Coordination, event handling
3. **Interface** (`component-name.ts`) - UI contracts for platform implementations
4. **Event Map** (`component-name-event-map.ts`) - Event type definitions

### **📋 Layer Responsibilities**

| Layer          | Purpose                                 | Key Rules                                                      |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Service**    | Platform-independent business logic     | ✅ Singleton exports, no UI dependencies, pure functions       |
| **Controller** | Pure coordination between services & UI | ✅ **NEVER implements View interfaces**, delegates to services |
| **Interface**  | Abstract UI APIs                        | ✅ Only UI-specific methods, no implementation                 |
| **Widget**     | Platform-specific UI                    | ✅ Implements interfaces, uses controllers/services            |

### **🚀 Implementation Pattern**

```typescript
// Service: Business Logic
export class ComponentStateService {
  calculateState(data: Input): Output {
    /* Pure logic */
  }
}
export const componentStateService = new ComponentStateService();

// Controller: Coordination Only
export class ComponentController {
  readonly events = new EventDispatcher<ComponentEventMap>();

  update(data: Input) {
    const result = componentStateService.calculateState(data);
    this.events.dispatch("updated", result);
  }
}
export const componentController = new ComponentController();

// Interface: UI Contract
export interface ComponentView {
  update(data: Output): void;
}
```

